  "statement": "Table order_items(order_id INTEGER, category TEXT, quantity INTEGER, unit_price INTEGER). Each row is one line of an order; an order can have several lines, even several lines in the same category.\n\nFor each category, return:\n- category\n- orders: the number of different orders that contain at least one line of that category\n- revenue: the sum of quantity * unit_price over its lines\nKeep only categories whose revenue is at least 100. Sort by revenue, highest first, then by category (A to Z).\n\nOutput: columns category, orders, revenue.\nConstraints: at most 10000 lines, quantity from 1 to 100, unit_price from 1 to 10000.\n\nExample\norder_items:\n  (1, 'books', 2, 15)\n  (1, 'games', 1, 60)\n  (2, 'books', 1, 80)\n  (2, 'music', 3, 10)\n  (3, 'games', 2, 25)\n  (3, 'games', 1, 5)\nOutput:\ngames|2|115\nbooks|2|110\n\n(music has a revenue of 30 only; games appears in orders 1 and 3, so orders is 2.)",
  "starter_code": "-- Table: order_items(order_id INTEGER, category TEXT, quantity INTEGER, unit_price INTEGER)\nSELECT category\nFROM order_items\n-- One row per category: category, orders, revenue\n;\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 2000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
